{
  "_about": "Named aces (Brian, 22 November 2026: a fighter group with a strong record earns a named ace; if he is shot down, the group's spirit drops for a month). src/campaign/aces.ts; the design director's rulings of 22 November 17:44Z and 17:45Z. 'on' is the switch for a new grand campaign. 'at': an ace is five victories, the record's own word. 'share': the share of his group's kills that falls to its leading pilot; the group names its ace when share x the aircraft it has downed since his count began reaches 'at', and his tally is that figure rounded. 0.042 (the design director's 19:26Z, D: the 56th Fighter Group's top ace, 28 of its 664.5 air kills; historian/air-ideas-aces-fog-1122.md), so a group names its ace at about 119 downed. 'risk': his chance to fall in a fight is the group's own loss share that day times this (1: no rate for aces' losses was found, so the design director's 17:44Z rule stands, 19:26Z). 'edge': while he flies, the player's group is worth this much more, inside the stories' edge cap like an honour (a DD knob). 'grief': the player's group's worth after he falls, for 'griefMonths' months counting the month he fell: HELD AT 1 (no effect) until the historian sources it (JG 52, the 56th Fighter Group). 'promote': victories for each step up in rank. 'navy': the ranks a carrier group's ace holds where his nation's fliers at sea held their navy's (America's naval aviators, the Fleet Air Arm; the plane thread's 20:13Z: a Navy ace was given an Army captain's rank). Names are invented, never a real man: 'guard' holds history's famous aces, never drawn.",
